# Why this file exists (added 2026-07-15 on t/live-stack):
#
# A clean `npm install` FAILS without it:
#
#   npm error Could not resolve dependency:
#   npm error peer react@"^16.8.0 || 17.x || 18.x" from react-simple-maps@3.0.0
#   npm error Conflicting peer dependency: react@18.3.1
#
# This project is on react 19.2.4 / next 16.2.9, but react-simple-maps@3.0.0 still declares a
# peer range that stops at react 18. The committed package-lock.json already resolves the two
# together (react 19.2.4 + react-simple-maps 3.0.0), i.e. it was generated with this flag — so
# without this file the lockfile installs on the original machine and nowhere else.
#
# react-simple-maps is currently pulled in ONLY by src/components/map/territory-map.tsx, which is
# not imported by any page or component. If that component stays unused, the real fix is to delete
# it and drop the dependency, after which this file can go too.
legacy-peer-deps=true
